+++ b/.omp/run/notes/RVThreads.md
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+The thread store is built: the new crate `yamt-review` stores threads in `threads.json` format 1. All 14 acceptance tests pass, along with fmt, clippy, the crate tests and `just arch-check`. I did not run `just mutants`.
+
+**summary**
+- New crate `crates/review` (`yamt-review`) with the IPC types (`thread_types.rs`), `threads.json` format 1 with all of its refusals and temp-file-plus-rename writes (`thread_file.rs`), and `ThreadStore` with open, list, add_thread, add_note, queue and unqueue (`thread_store.rs`).
+- It also has the two `pub(crate)` hooks for row 16: `queued()` and `record(message, Posting)`.
+- `yamt-range` gains `Range::entry`, `entries`, `compared` and `root`, plus the `Compared` struct.
+- `scripts/arch-check.sh` limits `yamt-review` to `yamt-range`, `yamt-gitio` and `yamt-merge-core` among yamt crates, never tauri, and lets `yamt-app` depend on it.
+
+**files_changed**
+- `crates/review/{Cargo.toml, AGENTS.md, src/lib.rs, src/thread_types.rs, src/thread_file.rs, src/thread_store.rs, tests/threads.rs}` (new)
+- `crates/range/src/lib.rs` (`Compared`)
+- `crates/range/src/open.rs` (granted by you: `Range` holds `entries` and `files` side by side, the four accessors, one unit test)
+- `crates/range/src/entries.rs` (granted by you: `entry` moved out of `FileAt`, new `entries_at`)
+- `crates/merge-core/src/line.rs` (granted by you: `Deserialize` on `LeftLine`/`RightLine` only)
+- `scripts/arch-check.sh`
+- `src-tauri/Cargo.toml` (the one path dependency line)
+- `Cargo.lock` (regenerated by cargo)
+
+**tests_added**
+- `tests/threads.rs`, all 14 names from the brief:
+  - `a_missing_file_is_an_empty_store_and_nothing_is_written`: the folder stays empty.
+  - `format_1_round_trips_every_body_and_posting_kind_and_a_session`: all 4 line kinds, both bodies, all 4postings, a session and a `draft_note` above u32. Typed values come back with the right file ids. After a write, the JSON equals the original apart from the one added message.
+  - `a_broken_file_names_line_and_column_and_is_left_unchanged`: the message says "line 3 column 3"; the bytes are unchanged and no temp file is left.
+  - `a_newer_format_is_refused_and_left_unchanged`: `NewerFormat{format:2}`, bytes unchanged.
+  - `repeated_ids_ids_at_or_above_next_and_threads_without_messages_are_broken`: five cases, each with its exact message, each file unchanged.
+  - `adding_writes_the_thread_with_its_first_message_and_new_ids`: ids 1/1, the stored path, the counters on disk, `written` inside the time window, a reopen matches, then the note gets message id 2.
+  - `ids_never_repeat_after_reopening`: counters 10/20 are honoured, and 11/21 after a reopen.
+  - `blank_text_is_refused_and_nothing_written`: add_thread, add_note and queue.
+  - `queue_keeps_the_edited_text_and_unqueue_drops_it`: the body is unchanged, a refused message becomes `Queued`, everything survives a reopen.
+  - `a_pending_message_cannot_be_queued_or_unqueued`
+  - `a_failed_write_changes_nothing_in_memory`: add_thread, add_note and queue each answer `WriteFailed`; memory and disk are unchanged; the next ids are still 2/2.
+  - `threads_on_paths_no_longer_listed_are_kept_on_every_write`: the file id is mapped back (c.txt is 2 in one range, 0 in the other). A hidden thread or message answers Unknown*. Writes made through the narrower range keep the hidden thread.
+  - `a_leftover_temp_file_is_ignored`
+  - `an_unknown_file_thread_or_message_is_its_error`
+- Unit tests in `thread_file.rs` (7): id at the counter (thread and message), a repeated message id across threads, counters at `u32::MAX`, format 0 is broken rather than newer, and taking the id just below `u32::MAX` is refused.
+- Unit tests in `thread_store.rs` (3): `queued_lists_queued_and_refused_messages_in_thread_then_message_order`, `record_writes_the_posting_and_keeps_it`, `record_on_an_unknown_message_is_unknown_message`.
+- `open.rs`: `the_accessors_answer_the_listed_rows_both_commits_and_the_work_tree`.
+
+**smoke_evidence**
+- `cargo fmt --check` → no output.
+- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` → `Finished`, no warnings.
+- `cargo test -p yamt-review -p yamt-range -p yamt-merge-core -p yamt-app`:
+  - yamt_review unit tests: `ok. 10 passed`; `tests/threads.rs`: `ok. 14 passed`
+  - yamt_range unit tests: `ok. 9 passed`; range.rs `ok. 11 passed`; lock.rs `ok. 3 passed`; listing_answers.rs `ok. 3 passed`
+  - yamt_app: `ok. 105 passed`
+  - yamt-merge-core: all test files ok
+- `just arch-check` → `arch-check: ok`.
+- Failing path, shown by hand: with `yamt-compare` added for a moment to `crates/review/Cargo.toml`, the output was `arch-check: yamt-review depends on yamt-range, yamt-gitio and yamt-merge-core only among yamt crates, and never on tauri, not: yamt-compare` with exit 1. I reverted it. No committed test exists for arch-check; none of the existing checks has one either.
+
+**deviations_from_brief**
+1. With your OK, `open.rs` and `entries.rs` were added to my files. The accessors live in `open.rs`, because `Range`'s fields are private there.
+2. With your OK, `Deserialize` was added to `LeftLine`/`RightLine` in `line.rs`. The TypeScript shape does not change.
+3. `Posting`, `MessageBody` and `Message` also derive `Deserialize`, because the file stores them as they are. As a result, a pending message's fields are written `draft_note` and `merge_request` in the file (the same snake_case as on the wire). The design's table said `draftNote`; using one type for both avoids a second copy of the shape.
+4. `written` and `draft_note` carry `#[specta(type = u32)]`, copied from `SideContent.bytes`.
+5. add_note, queue and unqueue answer `UnknownThread`/`UnknownMessage` for a thread on a path this range does not list. The window never sees those ids. The brief did not decide this.
+6. Text is stored as typed; it is trimmed only to check for blank. queue refuses blank text (`EmptyMessage`), as the design's §4 says.
+7. A new id that would leave a counter at `u32::MAX` is refused as `Broken` and nothing is written (the `tabs.json` rule).
+8. `queued()` returns a named `pub(crate) struct QueuedMessage { thread, message, path, line, text }` rather than a tuple. `queued` and `record` carry `#[cfg_attr(not(test), expect(dead_code, reason = …))]` until row 16 uses them.
+9. The `yamt-gitio` dependency is not added yet; row 16 adds it, and arch-check already allows it.
+10. Shared edits for you to make:
+    - root `Cargo.toml` `members`: add `"crates/review",`
+    - `[workspace.dependencies]`: add `yamt-review = { path = "crates/review" }`
+    - `src-tauri/Cargo.toml` could then use `yamt-review.workspace = true`; today the path line works because cargo treats it as a workspace member automatically.
+    - Docs I don't own need updating: `docs/architecture.md` / project-map (the `yamt-review` crate, the range accessors, the PM1 edge), `crates/range/AGENTS.md` (the accessors, and the split of `Range` into entries and files).
+
+**open_risks**
+- `thread_store.rs` `list` logs the `warn` about unlisted paths on every reply, not once per run (`crates/review/src/thread_store.rs` ≈ line 55).
+- Every change clones the whole file in memory, as `TabStore` does; that is fine at the expected sizes.
+- `just mutants` was not run on these lines; the asserts were written to kill the obvious mutants, including the four accessors.
\ No newline at end of file
