@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Owner skill: `skill://rust-conventions`. The user's review of a commit range: threads on its lines, stored per repository and commit pair (plan §2 #116, #117, #120): `lib.rs` (`Error`, `Result`), `thread_types.rs` (the IPC types `ThreadId`, `MessageId`, `ThreadLine` — `removed`/`added`/`unchangedOnLeft`/`unchangedOnRight`, 0-based `yamt_merge_core::{LeftLine, RightLine}`, the variant decides the column —, `MessageBody` `note`/`aiAnswer`, `Posting` `notQueued`/`queued`/`refused`/`pending`, `Message` (`written` seconds since 1970, a `u64` exported as number), `Thread` (`file` = the range's `RangeFileId`), `ThreadList`, `ThreadAdded`), `thread_file.rs` (`threads.json` format 1 in the pair folder: `format`, `nextThread`, `nextMessage`, `threads` [`id`, `path`, `line`, `session`, `messages` [`id`, `body`, `written`, `posting`]]; a thread stored by the entry's path, never its file id; refused as `Broken` when it does not parse (serde's line and column), repeats a thread or message id, holds an id not below its counter, a thread without messages, or a counter at `u32::MAX`; `NewerFormat` above 1; nothing written on a refusal; every write `threads.json.tmp` + rename, a leftover temp file never read), `thread_store.rs` (`ThreadStore`: open (missing = empty, nothing written), list (threads on paths the range lists, mapped back to their `RangeFileId`, in creation order; others kept on every write, left out with one `warn` line), add_thread, add_note, queue (`Queued` with the edited text, a refused message too), unqueue (`NotQueued`); blank text is `EmptyMessage`, a pending message is `MessagePending`; ids from the counters, never reused; the file written before memory changes, so a failed write changes nothing; `pub(crate)` `queued` (queued and refused messages in thread, then message order) and `record` for the sender). Depends on `yamt-range` (`Range::entry`, `Range::entries`) and `yamt-merge-core` among `yamt-*`, may use `yamt-gitio`, never tauri (`scripts/arch-check.sh`). Tests: unit tests in `thread_file.rs`, `thread_store.rs`; `tests/threads.rs` on real temp folders with a `Range` over a `yamt-conflict-repo` repository.
